  "mcpDecision": "Extend existing native/MCP facts with standalone fluent chains after a complete group/receiver-return audit. Preserve existing storage DTO and tool/schema/argument shapes. Each accepted chained registration points to its individual method-name token; source action contexts reuse that exact location from the primary value snapshot. This lets agents distinguish nested calls with a shared expression start offset without executing application code or claiming an active UI callback. Reuse storage/consumer, initial attachment, source action, snapshot/freshness/cancellation, isolation, response cap and exact read-only export infrastructure. No new tool or response member is required. Tool descriptions and client documentation explain chain locations and uncertainty.",
